visionOS has neither OpenGL nor OpenGL ES, so both arms of this fork name a key
the XROS SDK marks API_UNAVAILABLE(visionos) and libavcodec/videotoolbox.c fails
to compile outright. TARGET_OS_IPHONE is 1 on visionOS, which is what steers it
into the OpenGL ES arm. Metal is that platform's graphics interop and
kCVPixelBufferMetalCompatibilityKey is available there, so the new arm states
the same intent in the vocabulary the platform has.

Not upstreamed as of ffmpeg 8.1.2. Every other platform preprocesses to exactly
the code it did before: TARGET_OS_VISION is 0 on macOS, iOS and tvOS.

--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
@@ -816,7 +816,9 @@
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferIOSurfacePropertiesKey, io_surface_properties);
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferWidthKey, w);
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferHeightKey, h);
-#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+#if TARGET_OS_VISION
+    CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferMetalCompatibilityKey, kCFBooleanTrue);
+#elif TARGET_OS_IPHONE
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferOpenGLESCompatibilityKey, kCFBooleanTrue);
 #else
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferIOSurfaceOpenGLTextureCompatibilityKey, kCFBooleanTrue);
